            <ArticleTitle>Individual (f,t A)- and (f,t C)-Fullerene-Based Nickel(II) Glycinates: Protected Chiral Amino Acids Directly Linked to a Chiral π-Electron System.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2704-2708</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/anie.201609792</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stereoselective electrosynthesis of the first individual (f,t A)- and (f,t C)-1,4-fullerene derivatives with a non-inherently chiral functionalization pattern is described, as well as the first example of an optically pure protected primary amino acid directly linked to the fullerene through only the chiral α-amino-acid carbon atom. An application of an auxiliary chiral nickel-Schiff base moiety as derivatizing agent allowed separation of (f,t A)- and (f,t C)-1,4-fullerene derivatives using an achiral stationary phase, a separation which has never been done before.</AbstractText>
